{
  "$comment": "GENERATED from the real jscad-raspberrypi V1 MiniPiTFT(), PiTFT22(), PiTFT24(), PiTFT24({buttonWireYOffset: 0}) and HyperPixel4Rectangular(), plus Hat() itself, by reading parts[name].getBounds() and group.names inside a checkout of that repository (it is not an npm dependency here, which is why there is no scripts/generate-* companion - see raspberrypi.miniPiTFT.spec.js for the exact procedure). Do not hand-edit. All values are millimetres, Z-up. Unlike the core-016 touch fixture, EVERY factory here is called with NO BOARD: each one's own `if (piMotherBoard)` / `if (rpi)` guard then skips the attachment translate, so these bounds are already in the standalone frame this port emits and are compared absolutely, not lens-relative.",
